The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says all the reports are one issue. The desk's own
fingerprint (`src/lib/kb/fingerprint.ts`) says otherwise. It groups a report by **where it comes
from** (the product its reporter's tenant runs) and by the **server error code** in it, not by
the subject line.

<Callout kind="warn">

#4471 is more than one issue. Reports were merged on the subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). "Times moved by an hour" reads the
same on every product, so the other products' bugs went into the `sched-prod` ticket and
were closed with it.

</Callout>

## The issues, one ticket each

<IssueTickets ticket={4471} />

- **`sched-prod` · `E-TZ-114`**: shifts moved by one hour. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.
  Change #29 fixed it at 06:15, so its ticket is closed.
- **`tram-3` · `E-TZ-114`**: departure boards show every tram one hour late. It has the same
  code but a different product, so it is a different bug. Change #29 was a `sched-prod` fix,
  and nothing in the export shows that this one was fixed. The ticket stays open.
- **`rota-6` · `E-SYNC-04`**: the night shift is listed twice, one hour apart. It has a
  different code and a different product. The ticket stays open.

## How the count was made

1. One id, one report. The ticket system exports overlapping pages, so some reports appear
   twice. `uniqueById` drops the extra copies.
2. Place, not tag. Intake picks `product` from the subject line at night, and that is a
   guess. `placeOf` uses the reporter's tenant, so some reports tagged `sched-prod` move to
   `tram-3` or `rota-6`.
3. Server code, not client noise. `E-UI-…` and `E-NET-…` come from the client app. A report
   is filed under the server code (`E-TZ-…`, `E-SYNC-…`) next to them.
4. One person, one reporter. Letter case and `+tag` in an email address do not count as a
   new person.

## The first row

The #4471 page says the first report landed at 03:19. The export has an earlier row,
shown above: no reporter, no source, and a body that says `status: clean`. It is not a
customer report. It is the 03:12 job, which was merged into the ticket with everything else.

